# Line-ending policy (Ticket CRLF-FIX, per the FW-P1 diagnosis): history
# stores LF, and nothing may depend on the checkout machine's autocrlf
# setting again — a since-removed autocrlf=true once left ~500 worktree
# files CRLF and every diff unreadable. `text=auto` normalizes text files
# to LF in the repository regardless of local git config; binaries are
# auto-detected and left alone. Shell scripts additionally pin the
# WORKTREE to LF (eol=lf) — bash rejects CRLF scripts, so they must never
# be smudged to CRLF even on a machine that sets core.autocrlf=true.
#
# .ops/ keeps its own stricter .gitattributes (-text on captured
# artifacts): deeper-level attributes win, so byte-fidelity there is
# unaffected by the rules here.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
